IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wirc-core`

-- Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 (Vic) -- from the seat of the injured worker.
--
-- SEAT: the worker injured in employment connected with Victoria on or after 1 July 2014, and, under "If the worker
-- dies", the worker's dependants and close family members. "Am I covered? By when must I give notice and claim?
-- When is my claim taken to be accepted? How much are my weekly payments, and do they go on after 130 weeks? What
-- impairment benefit do I get? What does my family get if I die? Can I sue for damages, by when, and for how much?"
-- Each question is phrased as that person would ask it, on facts that person could state. The rules are in
-- wirc-core.l4; this module turns plain answers into the core's inputs and restates no rule.
--
-- FIGURES: the varied amounts for 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027 are in the core, from the Gazette notice of
-- 30 June 2026. A question that needs one answers NOTHING for a day outside those two years.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 (Vic) -- the injured worker's questions`

§§ `Am I covered (ss 37, 39, 40)`

-- `the injury results in death or severe injury` is built from the severe injury head only: the worker is the one
-- asking. A claim by dependants for a death is under "If the worker dies".
@export Am I entitled to compensation for my work injury under the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 (Vic) (ss 37, 39, 40)? Answers nothing for a mental injury before 31 March 2024, which the earlier text governs.
GIVEN `my employment is connected with Victoria` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment connected with Victoria: do you usually work in Victoria, or, if no one State, are you usually based here, or is your employer's principal place of business in Australia here (s 37(3))?
      `my injury is` IS A `Kind of injury` @desc Is your injury a physical injury, or a mental injury (one causing significant behavioural, cognitive or psychological dysfunction, diagnosed by a medical practitioner under the DSM)?
      `the day of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day the injury happened (ISO date, e.g. 2026-03-15)
      `my physical injury arose out of or in the course of my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a physical injury: did it arise out of or in the course of your employment, or (for a disease or gradual injury) is it due to the nature of your employment?
      `my mental injury arose predominantly out of or in the course of my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a mental injury: did it arise predominantly out of or in the course of your employment?
      `my mental injury was caused wholly or predominantly by reasonable management action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a mental injury: was it caused wholly or predominantly by management action taken on reasonable grounds and in a reasonable manner (an appraisal, discipline, transfer, dismissal and the like), a reasonable decision about such action, or your expectation of it (s 40(1))?
      `my mental injury was predominantly caused by work related stress or burnout from usual events` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a mental injury: was it predominantly caused by work related stress or burnout from events that may be considered usual or typical and reasonably expected in your duties (s 40(1A))?
      `my mental injury was predominantly caused by usual traumatic events in my duties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a mental injury: was it predominantly caused by traumatic events you experienced that may be considered usual or typical and reasonably expected in your duties (s 39(2A))?
      `my mental injury is a recurrence or aggravation of an earlier mental injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a mental injury: is it a recurrence, aggravation, acceleration, exacerbation or deterioration of a mental injury you already had?
      `my employment was the predominant cause of that recurrence or aggravation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: was your employment the predominant cause of the recurrence or aggravation (s 40(2A))?
      `my physical injury is a heart attack, stroke, disease or aggravation of an earlier condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a physical injury: is it a heart attack, a stroke, a disease, or a recurrence or aggravation of an injury or disease you already had (s 40(2), (3))?
      `my employment was a significant contributing factor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: was your employment a significant contributing factor to the injury (or the disease)?
      `it is proved my injury was deliberately self-inflicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been proved that your injury was deliberately or wilfully self-inflicted (s 40(4))?
      `it is proved my injury came from my serious and wilful misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been proved that your injury is attributable to your serious and wilful misconduct, such as being under the influence of alcohol or a drug (s 40(5))?
      `my injury is a severe injury of this kind` IS A `Severe injury head` @desc Is your injury one of the severe injuries in s 40(7) (brain injury, paraplegia, quadriplegia, amputation, severe burns, blindness, brachial plexus injury, internal injury), or none of these?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I entitled to compensation for my injury` `my employment is connected with Victoria` `my injury is` `the day of my injury` `my physical injury arose out of or in the course of my employment` `my mental injury arose predominantly out of or in the course of my employment` `my mental injury was caused wholly or predominantly by reasonable management action` `my mental injury was predominantly caused by work related stress or burnout from usual events` `my mental injury was predominantly caused by usual traumatic events in my duties` `my mental injury is a recurrence or aggravation of an earlier mental injury` `my employment was the predominant cause of that recurrence or aggravation` `my physical injury is a heart attack, stroke, disease or aggravation of an earlier condition` `my employment was a significant contributing factor` `it is proved my injury was deliberately self-inflicted` `it is proved my injury came from my serious and wilful misconduct` `my injury is a severe injury of this kind` MEANS
    `ss 37, 39, 40 -- the worker is entitled to compensation`
        `my employment is connected with Victoria`
        `my injury is`
        `the day of my injury`
        `my physical injury arose out of or in the course of my employment`
        `my mental injury arose predominantly out of or in the course of my employment`
        `my mental injury was caused wholly or predominantly by reasonable management action`
        `my mental injury was predominantly caused by work related stress or burnout from usual events`
        `my mental injury was predominantly caused by usual traumatic events in my duties`
        `my mental injury is a recurrence or aggravation of an earlier mental injury`
        `my employment was the predominant cause of that recurrence or aggravation`
        `my physical injury is a heart attack, stroke, disease or aggravation of an earlier condition`
        `my employment was a significant contributing factor`
        `it is proved my injury was deliberately self-inflicted`
        `it is proved my injury came from my serious and wilful misconduct`
        (`s 40(7) -- is a severe injury` `my injury is a severe injury of this kind`)

§§ `Notice of injury and the claim (ss 18, 20, 75, 178)`

@export By what day must I give my employer notice of my injury (s 18(1))? Entering the details in the workplace register of injuries counts as notice (s 18(3)).
GIVEN `the day I became aware of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day you became aware of the injury (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must I give my employer notice of my injury` `the day I became aware of my injury` MEANS
    `s 18(1) -- the last day for notice of injury` `the day I became aware of my injury`

@export I gave notice of my injury on a certain day: can I still recover compensation (s 18(5)-(7))?
GIVEN `the day I became aware of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day you became aware of the injury (ISO date)
      `the day I gave notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave your employer notice, or the details were entered in the register of injuries (ISO date)
      `the time for notice was waived or extended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has WorkSafe (the Authority) or your employer's self-insurer waived or extended the 30-day time limit?
      `why my notice was late` IS A `Reason for late notice` @desc If the notice was late, was it because of ignorance or a mistake, undue influence or duress, being absent from Victoria, or none of these?
GIVETH A `Notice outcome`
`What follows from when I gave notice of my injury` `the day I became aware of my injury` `the day I gave notice` `the time for notice was waived or extended` `why my notice was late` MEANS
    `s 18(5)-(7) -- the effect of the time notice was given` `the day I became aware of my injury` `the day I gave notice` `the time for notice was waived or extended` `why my notice was late`

@export By what day must my claim be made (s 20(8))? A death claim within 2 years of the death, a medical and like services claim within 6 months of the service; a weekly payments claim "as soon as practicable" (no day: nothing); an impairment benefit claim has no limit in s 20(8) (nothing).
GIVEN `my claim is` IS A `Kind of claim` @desc Is this a claim for weekly payments, for compensation for the death of a worker, for medical and like services, or for an impairment benefit?
      `the day of the worker's death` IS A DATE @desc For a death claim: the day the worker died (ISO date; any date otherwise)
      `the day of the service` IS A DATE @desc For a medical and like services claim: the day of the service (ISO date; any date otherwise)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By what day must my claim be made` `my claim is` `the day of the worker's death` `the day of the service` MEANS
    `s 20(8) -- the last day to make the claim` `my claim is` `the day of the worker's death` `the day of the service`

@export By what day must WorkSafe or the self-insurer decide my claim for weekly payments (s 75(1))?
GIVEN `the day my claim was received` IS A DATE @desc The day WorkSafe (the Authority) or the self-insurer received your claim (ISO date)
      `my claim came with a medical certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your claim come with a medical certificate under s 25?
      `the day my medical certificate was received` IS A DATE @desc If not: the day the medical certificate was received (ISO date; any date otherwise)
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must my weekly payments claim be decided` `the day my claim was received` `my claim came with a medical certificate` `the day my medical certificate was received` MEANS
    `s 75(1) -- the last day for a decision on a weekly payments claim` `the day my claim was received` `my claim came with a medical certificate` `the day my medical certificate was received`

@export Is my claim for weekly payments taken to be accepted because no written decision was given in time (s 75(1))?
GIVEN `the day my claim was received` IS A DATE @desc The day WorkSafe (the Authority) or the self-insurer received your claim (ISO date)
      `my claim came with a medical certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your claim come with a medical certificate under s 25?
      `the day my medical certificate was received` IS A DATE @desc If not: the day the medical certificate was received (ISO date; any date otherwise)
      `I have been given a written decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been given written notice of a decision to accept or reject the claim?
      `the day I was given the written decision` IS A DATE @desc If so: the day you were given it (ISO date; any date otherwise)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (ISO date)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my weekly payments claim taken to be accepted` `the day my claim was received` `my claim came with a medical certificate` `the day my medical certificate was received` `I have been given a written decision` `the day I was given the written decision` `today` MEANS
    `s 75(1) -- the claim is deemed accepted`
        (`s 75(1) -- the last day for a decision on a weekly payments claim` `the day my claim was received` `my claim came with a medical certificate` `the day my medical certificate was received`)
        `I have been given a written decision`
        `the day I was given the written decision`
        `today`

@export By what day must my weekly payments begin once my claim is accepted (s 178(3))?
GIVEN `the day my claim was accepted` IS A DATE @desc The day your claim for weekly payments was accepted (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must my weekly payments begin` `the day my claim was accepted` MEANS
    `s 178(3) -- the last day for weekly payments to begin` `the day my claim was accepted`

§§ `Provisional payments for a mental injury (Part 5 Division 10)`

-- Situation: the worker has made a claim for compensation for a mental injury.
@export I have claimed for a mental injury: can I have the reasonable costs of treatment paid as provisional payments while my claim is decided (s 263B)?
GIVEN `the day I made my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you made your claim for the mental injury (ISO date)
      `a claim for the same mental injury and circumstances was decided before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has WorkSafe or the self-insurer already decided a claim for the same mental injury and circumstances?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can I get provisional payments for my mental injury` `the day I made my claim` `a claim for the same mental injury and circumstances was decided before` MEANS
    `s 263B -- the worker is entitled to provisional payments` `the day I made my claim` `a claim for the same mental injury and circumstances was decided before`

@export Until what day are my provisional payments for a mental injury payable (s 263I)?
GIVEN `the day I was found entitled to provisional payments` IS A DATE @desc The day WorkSafe or the self-insurer decided under s 75A that you are entitled to provisional payments (ISO date)
      `my claim has been accepted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your claim for the mental injury been accepted?
      `the day my claim was accepted` IS A DATE @desc If so: the day it was accepted (ISO date; any date otherwise)
GIVETH A DATE
`Until what day are my provisional payments payable` `the day I was found entitled to provisional payments` `my claim has been accepted` `the day my claim was accepted` MEANS
    `s 263I -- the day provisional payments end` `the day I was found entitled to provisional payments` `my claim has been accepted` `the day my claim was accepted`

§§ `Weekly payments (Part 5 Divisions 2 and 3)`

-- Situation: the worker is incapacitated for work by an accepted injury.
@export Which entitlement period is this week of my weekly payments in: the first (weeks 1-13), the second (weeks 14-130), or after (s 152)?
GIVEN `the number of this week of weekly payments` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting every week for which weekly payments have been paid or are payable, for all or part of the week, whether or not consecutive: which number is this week (1 for the first)?
GIVETH AN `Entitlement period`
`Which entitlement period is this week in` `the number of this week of weekly payments` MEANS
    `s 152 -- the entitlement period of week` `the number of this week of weekly payments`

@export How much are my weekly payments for this week (ss 161, 162, 163(2), 165(5))? 95 per cent of pre-injury earnings in the first 13 weeks, 80 per cent after, less 80 per cent of what you now earn, capped at twice the State average weekly earnings; nil after 130 weeks unless s 163 or s 165 applies.
GIVEN `a day in the week` IS A DATE @desc A day in the week you are asking about (ISO date); the cap for that financial year is used (1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027 only)
      `the number of this week of weekly payments` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting every week for which weekly payments have been paid or are payable, whether or not consecutive: which number is this week (1 for the first)?
      `my pre-injury average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your pre-injury average weekly earnings under s 153, as indexed, in dollars a week
      `the deductible amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly value of non-pecuniary benefits (car, housing, health insurance, education fees) your employer still provides, in dollars (0 if none)
      `I have a current work capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you return to work in suitable employment, though not your pre-injury job?
      `my current weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What you earn now each week, in dollars (0 if nothing)
      `WorkSafe has made the s 163(1) determination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After 130 weeks: has WorkSafe or the self-insurer determined that you have no current work capacity, likely indefinitely, and more than 20 per cent whole person impairment?
      `my s 165 application was approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After 130 weeks: was your application under s 165 (working at least 15 hours a week) approved?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much are my weekly payments this week` `a day in the week` `the number of this week of weekly payments` `my pre-injury average weekly earnings` `the deductible amount` `I have a current work capacity` `my current weekly earnings` `WorkSafe has made the s 163(1) determination` `my s 165 application was approved` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the varied amount` `twice the State average weekly earnings` `on` `a day in the week`
    WHEN JUST `the cap` THEN JUST (`ss 161-165 -- the weekly payment` `the cap` `the number of this week of weekly payments` `my pre-injury average weekly earnings` `the deductible amount` `I have a current work capacity` `my current weekly earnings` `WorkSafe has made the s 163(1) determination` `my s 165 application was approved`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@export Do I meet the conditions for my weekly payments to go on after the second entitlement period (130 weeks) because I cannot work (s 163(1))? The determination is WorkSafe's or the self-insurer's; nothing if you were already paid past 130 weeks before 31 March 2024 (s 625(2)).
GIVEN `I have no current work capacity, likely indefinitely` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you unable to return to any work, and likely to stay so indefinitely?
      `my whole person impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your whole person impairment from your compensable injuries, in per cent
      `I was paid past the second entitlement period before 31 March 2024` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you, immediately before 31 March 2024, already receiving weekly payments after the end of the second entitlement period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my weekly payments go on after 130 weeks because I cannot work` `I have no current work capacity, likely indefinitely` `my whole person impairment` `I was paid past the second entitlement period before 31 March 2024` MEANS
    IF `I was paid past the second entitlement period before 31 March 2024`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`s 163(1) -- the conditions for weekly payments after the second entitlement period are met` `I have no current work capacity, likely indefinitely` `my whole person impairment`)

@export Do I meet the conditions for my weekly payments to go on after the second entitlement period (130 weeks) while I work (s 165(4))? At least 15 hours a week, earnings at least the varied minimum, unable to do more work indefinitely, and more than 20 per cent whole person impairment.
GIVEN `the day of my application` IS A DATE @desc The day of your application under s 165 (ISO date); the minimum earnings for that financial year are used (1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027 only)
      `the hours I work each week` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours you work each week, in employment or self-employment
      `my current weekly earnings with non-pecuniary benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc What you earn each week, with any non-pecuniary benefits, in dollars
      `I cannot take on more work, likely indefinitely` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Because of the injury, are you, and likely to stay, unable to take on further work that would increase your earnings?
      `my whole person impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your whole person impairment from your compensable injuries, in per cent
      `I was paid past the second entitlement period before 31 March 2024` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you, immediately before 31 March 2024, already receiving weekly payments after the end of the second entitlement period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my weekly payments go on after 130 weeks while I work` `the day of my application` `the hours I work each week` `my current weekly earnings with non-pecuniary benefits` `I cannot take on more work, likely indefinitely` `my whole person impairment` `I was paid past the second entitlement period before 31 March 2024` MEANS
    IF `I was paid past the second entitlement period before 31 March 2024`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the varied amount` `the minimum current weekly earnings in ss 164 and 165` `on` `the day of my application`
         WHEN JUST `the minimum` THEN JUST (`s 165(4) -- the conditions for continuing weekly payments while working are met` `the minimum` `the hours I work each week` `my current weekly earnings with non-pecuniary benefits` `I cannot take on more work, likely indefinitely` `my whole person impairment`)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@export Does my age limit my weekly payments: do they stop at retirement (pension) age, or am I limited to 130 weeks because I was injured within 130 weeks before it or after it (ss 169, 171)?
GIVEN `the day of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day the injury happened (ISO date)
      `the day I reach pension age` IS A DATE @desc The day you reach age pension age under the Social Security Act 1991 (Cth) (ISO date)
GIVETH AN `Age limit`
`Does my age limit my weekly payments` `the day of my injury` `the day I reach pension age` MEANS
    `ss 169, 171 -- the age limit on weekly payments` `the day of my injury` `the day I reach pension age`

@export How many days' notice must I be given before my weekly payments are stopped or cut (s 189)? Nothing where s 189 does not apply (fewer than 12 weeks of payments, or no certificate of capacity).
GIVEN `the continuous weeks I have been paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many continuous weeks have you received weekly payments?
      `I have given a certificate of capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given your employer, WorkSafe or the self-insurer a certificate of capacity under s 167?
      `the reason payments are ending or being cut` IS A `Reason for ending or reducing weekly payments` @desc Why: the end of the second entitlement period (130 weeks), no longer qualifying for s 165 payments, your employer withdrawing your job while on s 165 payments, or another reason?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How many days notice must I be given before my weekly payments stop or are cut` `the continuous weeks I have been paid` `I have given a certificate of capacity` `the reason payments are ending or being cut` MEANS
    `s 189 -- the days of notice before weekly payments are ended or reduced` `the continuous weeks I have been paid` `I have given a certificate of capacity` `the reason payments are ending or being cut`

§§ `Impairment benefit (Part 5 Divisions 4 and 5)`

-- Situation: the worker has a permanent impairment from the injury.
@export From what day can I make a claim for an impairment benefit (s 197(2))? Twelve months after the injury, unless it has stabilised or is one of the listed kinds.
GIVEN `the day of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day the injury happened (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`From what day can I claim an impairment benefit` `the day of my injury` MEANS
    `s 197(2) -- the first day an impairment benefit claim can be made` `the day of my injury`

@export Can I make my claim for an impairment benefit on this day (s 197(2), (3))? Before 12 months only if the injury has stabilised (WorkSafe or the self-insurer may then receive it) or it is industrial deafness, an eligible progressive disease, a further EPD injury, a serious lung injury or a lung transplant injury.
GIVEN `the day of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day the injury happened (ISO date)
      `the day I would claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you would make the claim (ISO date)
      `my injury is of a listed kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your injury industrial deafness, an eligible progressive disease, a further EPD injury, a serious lung injury, or one treated with lung transplant surgery?
      `my injury has stabilised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your injury stabilised?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can I make my impairment benefit claim on this day` `the day of my injury` `the day I would claim` `my injury is of a listed kind` `my injury has stabilised` MEANS
    `s 197(2), (3) -- an impairment benefit claim can be made on that day` `the day of my injury` `the day I would claim` `my injury is of a listed kind` `my injury has stabilised`

@export How much is my impairment benefit (non-economic loss) lump sum for a permanent physical impairment (ss 210, 211)? Nil under 10 per cent; capped at the maximum. Uses the amounts for the injury day (rating up to 70) or the calculation day (over 70), 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027 only.
GIVEN `my impairment benefit rating` IS A NUMBER @desc Your impairment benefit rating under s 210(2), in per cent
      `how my rating is described` IS A `How the rating is described` @desc Is the rating a modified whole person impairment from Schedule 3, a modified spinal impairment, a spinal impairment, or any other whole person impairment?
      `the day of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day the injury happened (ISO date)
      `the day the amount is calculated` IS A DATE @desc The day the amount is calculated (ISO date)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much is my impairment benefit for a physical impairment` `my impairment benefit rating` `how my rating is described` `the day of my injury` `the day the amount is calculated` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the figures year for` (`s 210(1) -- the relevant date` `my impairment benefit rating` `the day of my injury` `the day the amount is calculated`)
    WHEN JUST `y` THEN JUST (`s 211(2) -- the non-economic loss for permanent impairment` `y` `my impairment benefit rating` `how my rating is described`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@export How much is my impairment benefit (non-economic loss) lump sum for a permanent psychiatric impairment (s 212)? Nil under 30 per cent.
GIVEN `my psychiatric impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your degree of permanent psychiatric impairment, in per cent
      `the day of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day the injury happened (ISO date)
      `the day the amount is calculated` IS A DATE @desc The day the amount is calculated (ISO date)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much is my impairment benefit for a psychiatric impairment` `my psychiatric impairment` `the day of my injury` `the day the amount is calculated` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the figures year for` (`s 210(1) -- the relevant date` `my psychiatric impairment` `the day of my injury` `the day the amount is calculated`)
    WHEN JUST `y` THEN JUST (`s 212 -- the non-economic loss for permanent psychiatric impairment` `y` `my psychiatric impairment`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@export I have several injuries from one occasion, or several kinds of non-economic loss from one injury: what is my total after the limit (ss 217, 219)?
GIVEN `the total of my amounts` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum of the non-economic loss amounts for the injuries or kinds of loss, in dollars
      `the relevant date` IS A DATE @desc The relevant date: the day of the injury, or the day of calculation if the rating is over 70 per cent (ISO date)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is my total impairment benefit after the limit` `the total of my amounts` `the relevant date` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the figures year for` `the relevant date`
    WHEN JUST `y` THEN JUST (`s 217 -- the non-economic loss after the limit` `y` `the total of my amounts`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `If the worker dies (Part 5 Division 8)`

-- Situation: a worker has died of a work injury. The asker is a dependant or a close family member. READING: the
-- amounts in force on the day of the death are used (the Act does not say which day; NOTES.md finding 3).
@export The worker has died of a work injury: how much is my share of the lump sum as a dependent partner or dependent child (s 236)? Nothing where the share is left to the court, WorkSafe or the self-insurer (s 236(6), s 237).
GIVEN `the day of the death` IS A DATE @desc The day the worker died (ISO date)
      `I am` IS A `Dependant's place` @desc Are you a dependent partner (wholly or mainly dependent on the worker's earnings, or living with the worker) or a dependent child?
      `the number of dependent partners` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent partners did the worker leave?
      `the number of dependent children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent children (under 16, or under 25 and studying or apprenticed full-time) did the worker leave?
      `every dependent child is an orphan child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is every dependent child an orphan child (the other parent died first, or was not a dependent partner and did not support the child)?
      `the worker left a partially dependent partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the worker leave a partner who was only partly dependent on the worker's earnings?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much is my share of the lump sum for the worker's death` `the day of the death` `I am` `the number of dependent partners` `the number of dependent children` `every dependent child is an orphan child` `the worker left a partially dependent partner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the figures year for` `the day of the death`
    WHEN JUST `y` THEN `s 236 -- the share of the lump sum` `y` `I am` `the number of dependent partners` `the number of dependent children` `every dependent child is an orphan child` `the worker left a partially dependent partner`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@export The worker has died of a work injury: how much compensation for grief and loss do I get as a close family member (s 237A)?
GIVEN `the day of the death` IS A DATE @desc The day the worker died (ISO date)
      `I was the worker's` IS A `Relationship to the worker` @desc Were you the worker's partner, parent, guardian, step-parent, grandparent, sibling or step-sibling, or a person the worker was a parent, step-parent or guardian to, or none of these?
      `I had a genuine personal relationship with the worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a genuine personal relationship with the worker when they died?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much grief and loss compensation do I get` `the day of the death` `I was the worker's` `I had a genuine personal relationship with the worker` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the figures year for` `the day of the death`
    WHEN JUST `y` THEN JUST (`s 237A(1) -- the grief and loss amount` `y` `I was the worker's` `I had a genuine personal relationship with the worker`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `Damages at common law (Part 7 Division 2)`

-- Situation: the worker wants to sue for damages for the injury.
@export From what day can I apply to sue for damages on the ground that I have a serious injury, without an impairment determination (s 328(2)(b))? At least 18 months after the event.
GIVEN `the day of the event that caused my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day of the event or circumstance that gave rise to the injury (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`From what day can I apply on the ground of serious injury` `the day of the event that caused my injury` MEANS
    `s 328(2)(b) -- the first day a serious injury application can be made` `the day of the event that caused my injury`

@export By what day must WorkSafe or the self-insurer answer my serious injury application (s 330(1))? 120 days, not counting 24 December to 9 January (s 329A).
GIVEN `the day my application was received` IS A DATE @desc The day WorkSafe or the self-insurer received your serious injury application (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must my serious injury application be answered` `the day my application was received` MEANS
    `s 330(1) -- the last day to advise on a serious injury application` `the day my application was received`

@export Is my injury taken to be a serious injury so I can sue for damages, or do I need WorkSafe's certificate or a court's leave (ss 330(3), 335)?
GIVEN `my impairment assessed before my application` IS A NUMBER @desc Your degree of impairment as assessed under Division 4 of Part 5 before your application, in per cent (0 if none)
      `the day my application was received` IS A DATE @desc The day WorkSafe or the self-insurer received your serious injury application (ISO date)
      `I have been given written advice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been given written advice on your application under s 330(1)?
      `the day I was given the advice` IS A DATE @desc If so: the day you were given it (ISO date; any date otherwise)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (ISO date)
GIVETH A `Serious injury gateway`
`Is my injury taken to be a serious injury` `my impairment assessed before my application` `the day my application was received` `I have been given written advice` `the day I was given the advice` `today` MEANS
    `ss 330, 335 -- the serious injury gateway` `my impairment assessed before my application` `the day my application was received` `I have been given written advice` `the day I was given the advice` `today`

@export By what day must I apply to a court for leave to bring proceedings for damages (s 335(2)(d)(i))? 30 days after receiving the advice, not counting 24 December to 9 January (s 329A); later only with WorkSafe's consent (s 337(1)).
GIVEN `the day I received the advice` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the written advice under s 330(1) (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must I apply to the court for leave` `the day I received the advice` MEANS
    `s 335(2)(d)(i) -- the last day to apply to a court for leave` `the day I received the advice`

@export If I rely on loss of earning capacity for a serious injury, do I meet the Act's requirements: a loss of 40 per cent or more, continuing permanently, and no capacity to earn more than 60 per cent (s 325(2)(e)-(g))? Whether the injury is "serious" is still for WorkSafe or the court; nothing for a worker under 26 at the injury or in Schedule 2 item 1.
GIVEN `I was under 26 at the injury or am in Schedule 2 item 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you under 26 at the injury, or are you a worker of the kind in item 1 of Schedule 2?
      `my yearly income now` IS A NUMBER @desc The greater of what you now earn a year from personal exertion and what you could earn in suitable employment, in dollars
      `my yearly income without the injury` IS A NUMBER @desc What you earned or could have earned a year from personal exertion over the 3 years before and after the injury, as most fairly reflects your earning capacity had the injury not occurred, in dollars
      `my yearly income from any work I could do after rehabilitation` IS A NUMBER @desc What you could earn a year in any employment, including alternative or additional work, after rehabilitation or retraining, in dollars
      `my loss will continue permanently at 40 per cent or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will your loss of earning capacity continue permanently to cause a financial loss of 40 per cent or more?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Do I meet the loss of earning capacity requirements` `I was under 26 at the injury or am in Schedule 2 item 1` `my yearly income now` `my yearly income without the injury` `my yearly income from any work I could do after rehabilitation` `my loss will continue permanently at 40 per cent or more` MEANS
    `s 325(2)(e)-(g) -- the loss of earning capacity requirements are met` `I was under 26 at the injury or am in Schedule 2 item 1` `my yearly income now` `my yearly income without the injury` `my yearly income from any work I could do after rehabilitation` `my loss will continue permanently at 40 per cent or more`

@export How much pecuniary loss damages (loss of earnings and earning capacity) can a court award me (s 340(a))? Nil under the threshold, no more than the maximum, both as at the date of the award (1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027 only).
GIVEN `the damages assessed before reductions` IS A NUMBER @desc The total pecuniary loss damages assessed, before any reduction for contributory negligence or for compensation paid, in dollars
      `the day of the award` IS A DATE @desc The day of the award (ISO date)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much pecuniary loss damages can I be awarded` `the damages assessed before reductions` `the day of the award` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the figures year for` `the day of the award`
    WHEN JUST `y` THEN JUST (`s 340 -- the damages that may be awarded` (`the varied amount` `the s 340(a)(i) pecuniary loss threshold` `for` `y`) (`the varied amount` `the s 340(a)(ii) pecuniary loss maximum` `for` `y`) `the damages assessed before reductions`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@export How much damages for pain and suffering can a court award me (s 340(b))? Nil under the threshold, no more than the maximum, both as at the date of the award (1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027 only).
GIVEN `the damages assessed before reductions` IS A NUMBER @desc The total damages for pain and suffering assessed, before any reduction for contributory negligence or for compensation paid, in dollars
      `the day of the award` IS A DATE @desc The day of the award (ISO date)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much damages for pain and suffering can I be awarded` `the damages assessed before reductions` `the day of the award` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the figures year for` `the day of the award`
    WHEN JUST `y` THEN JUST (`s 340 -- the damages that may be awarded` (`the varied amount` `the s 340(b)(i) pain and suffering threshold` `for` `y`) (`the varied amount` `the s 340(b)(ii) pain and suffering maximum` `for` `y`) `the damages assessed before reductions`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
